rd graduate school at the University of Louisiana at Lafayette. Before you begin your application, we encourage you to review the information provided to ensure you know what to expect throughout each step of the process.\nChoose Your Graduate Program | Start by exploring our graduate programs to find the one the best aligns with your academic and professional goals.\nReview Your Program's Admission Requirements & Deadlines | Because admission requirements and deadlines can vary depending on your program of your choice, it's important you review them, so you know what you need to submit and when your complete application is due.\nGather Your Application Materials | Give yourself time to gather the necessary documents to complete your application. All applications require the submission of official transcripts. Additional documents can include letters of recommendation, test scores, resumes, and writing samples to name a few.\nAre You an International Applicant? | International students may have additional requirements for admission. Please review the English language proficiency requirements, foreign credential evaluation, I-20 requirements, and visa information before applying.\nReview the Application Process | Create your account, submit your application, upload necessary documents, and then what? Review the application process so you know what to expect throughout the admissions process.\nReady to Apply? | You've chosen your program, reviewed the admission requirements and deadlines, and gathered your application materials, you're ready to apply!\nRequest Information\nVisit Campus\nApply\n337-482-6965\ngradschool@louisiana.edu\nMartin Hall, Suite 332\n104 University Circle\nLafayette, LA 70503\nGraduate Programs\nAdmissions\nBefore You Apply\nAdmission Requirements\nRequired Documents and Application Fee\nInternational Applicants\nPrograms & Deadlines\nThe Application Process\nApplication Checklist\nApply Now\nAfter You Apply\nTuition & Funding\nCampus & Communit